/E (The symbolism also reflects one of the central truths long taught within Free Gardenery: that growth occurs slowly, quietly, and organically. Gardens cannot be forced into greatness overnight. They must be cultivated patiently through discipline, care, and wisdom. Likewise, the human soul cannot be perfected through domination or ambition, but only through steady cultivation of Love, Wisdom, Harmony, and Truth.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
